        "---\n",
        "title: \"Will open bibliographic metadata work in RAG?\"\n",
        "subtitle: \"PhD Program in Information Science\"\n",
        "author: \"Poppy Riddle\"\n",
        "format: \n",
        "  revealjs:\n",
        "    theme: [default, www/custom.scss]\n",
        "    progress: true\n",
        "    slide-number: true\n",
        "    preview-links: auto\n",
        "    embed-resources: false\n",
        "    scrollable: true\n",
        "lightbox: true\n",
        "editor: visual\n",
        "background-transition: fade\n",
        "project:\n",
        "  execute-dir: project\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "<!--# https://htmlcolorcodes.com/color-chart/web-safe-color-chart/ -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!--# more helpful stuff: https://emilhvitfeldt.com/blog -->\n",
        "\n",
        "<!--# plugins should you want them: https://github.com/hakimel/reveal.js/wiki/Plugins,-Tools-and-Hardware -->\n",
        "\n",
        "# Hello\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "Why am I doing this work?\n",
        "\n",
        "- background\n",
        "- physical tool making to digital tool making\n",
        "- lack of science and evidence in design\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "## Presentation overview\n",
        "\n",
        "-   Introduction & Background\n",
        "-   Theoretical Framework\n",
        "-   Problem Statement, Purpose, & RQs\n",
        "-   Methods\n",
        "-   Results\n",
        "-   Implications\n",
        "-   Recommendations\n",
        "-   Contributions\n",
        "-   Future Research\n",
        "\n",
        "# Introduction & Background\n",
        "\n",
        "## What is Bibliographic Metadata?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "- Open sources of metadata\n",
        "- the data about scholarly resources, books, articles, datasets, \n",
        "- used for resource location, retrieval, identification, commpliance, preservation\n",
        "- differences between two\n",
        "- OpenAlex pulls from Crossref\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: columns\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "![](images/Crossref_Logo.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"40%\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "![](images/OpenAlex_logo.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"100%\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: columns\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "![](images/crossref_metadata_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"100%\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "![](images/openalex_metadata_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"100%\"}\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "## [Errors and Noise]{.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "- Title and abstract, why are these significant?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "### Crossref\n",
        "\n",
        "Abstract metadata from <https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1103/physrevd.110.036015>\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/abstract_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "Or, another example from <https://api.crossref.org/works/10.33024/hjk.v15i1.3791>:\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/abstract2_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "Or one that contains geometric shapes, from <https://api.crossref.org/works/10.1108/eemcs-04-2022-0108>\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/abstract3_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "### OpenAlex\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/abstract_tags_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\"} [Transformation of abstracts from Crossref (left) to OpenAlex (right)]{.blue .smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/abstract_crammed_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\"} [Two languages in one abstract]{.blue .smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/abstract_german_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\"} [Transformation of languages]{.blue .smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/abstract_encodings_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\"} [Encodings added to the OpenAlex version]{.blue .smaller}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Conversational Search {.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "bibliographic metadata of scholarly resources: journal articles, book chapters, conference proceedings have the most textual data with abstracts\n",
        "\n",
        "Conversational search using RAG: ScopusAI, WoS Research Assistant, ProQuest One, PrimoVE Research Assistant\n",
        "\n",
        "While they are using proprietary databases, can we use open-databases and create open-source conversational search?\n",
        "\n",
        "- Title and Abstract - why are these significant?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "![Example of a conversational search interface, PrimoVE Research Assistant](images/PRA_Overview2_overlays.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"100%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "[image source: https://knowledge.exlibrisgroup.com/Primo/Product_Documentation/020Primo_VE/Primo_VE\\_(English)/015_Getting_Started_with_Primo_Research_Assistant]{.small}\n",
        "\n",
        "![Example of keyword search interface](images/novanet_overlay.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"100%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## [Metadata Quality]{.scrollable}\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "prior research\n",
        "- Coverage & Availability (Alonso-Álvarez & van Eck 2024)\n",
        "- Coverage, Accuracy, Completeness (Céspedes et al., 2024; Visser et al., 2021)\n",
        "- Coverage (Culbert et al., 2024)\n",
        "- Completeness (Delgado-Quirós & Ortega 2024)\n",
        "- Availability (Eck & Waltman 2022)\n",
        "- Completeness, Consistency, Conformity, Access (Király et al. 2019)\n",
        "- Availability & Completeness (Kramer & de Jonge 2022)\n",
        "- Accuracy (Mongeon et al., 2025)\n",
        "- Accuracy (Sainte-Marie et al., 2025)\n",
        "- Coverage & Accuracy (Schares 2024)\n",
        "- Accuracy, Consistency, Completeness (Shi et al., 2023)\n",
        "- Coverage (Simard et al., 2024)\n",
        "- Accessibility & Coverage (Zhang et al., 2024)\n",
        "\n",
        "- Yasser et al., (2011) ‘poorly created metadata records result in poor retrieval and limit accessibility to collections’. They classified problems as “Incorrect Values, Incorrect Elements, Missing Information, Information Loss, and Inconsistent Value Representation ” (Yasser, 2011, p. 51). also Bruce and Hillman; Delgado-Quirós & Ortega\n",
        "\n",
        "NLP defined noise from Wu et al\n",
        "- semantic: off-topic, deviating from intended meaning, ambiguous terms\n",
        "- datatype: links, encodings, urls, code\n",
        "- illegal sentence: incoherent or grammatically incorrect - OCR\n",
        "- counterfactual: factual errors\n",
        "- supportive: high semantic relevance, but lacking answer\n",
        "- orthographic: writing errors, typos, truncation\n",
        "- prior: false assumptions or premises\n",
        "Beneficial and Harmful!\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "![](images/prior_metadata_1.svg){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"70%\" .lightbox .center}\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "### An LIS Perspective\n",
        "\n",
        "Yasser et al., (2011)\n",
        "\n",
        "-   Incorrect values\n",
        "-   Incorrect elements\n",
        "-   Missing information\n",
        "-   Information loss\n",
        "-   Inconsistent value representation\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "### An NLP Perspective\n",
        "\n",
        "Noise classification from Wu et al., (2025)\n",
        "\n",
        "-   Semantic\n",
        "-   Datatype\n",
        "-   Illegal sentence\n",
        "-   Counterfactual\n",
        "-   Supportive\n",
        "-   Orthographic\n",
        "-   Prior\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "### A Combined Perspective\n",
        "\n",
        "| **Quality Classification**        | **Source**          |\n",
        "|-----------------------------------|---------------------|\n",
        "| Semantic noise                    | Wu et al., 2025     |\n",
        "| Datatype noise                    | Wu et al., 2025     |\n",
        "| Incorrect values                  | Yasser et al., 2011 |\n",
        "| Incorrect elements                | Yasser et al., 2011 |\n",
        "| Missing information               | Yasser et al., 2011 |\n",
        "| Information loss                  | Yasser et al., 2011 |\n",
        "| Inconsistent value representation | Yasser et al., 2011 |\n",
        "\n",
        ": <br> <!--# https://tablesgenerator.com/markdown_tables -->\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Metadata and RAG?\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "LLM-based chat application ![](images/LLM_chat.svg){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"120%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "Retrieval-augmented generation ![](images/rag_basic.svg){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"160%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Theoretical Framework\n",
        "\n",
        "## The Framework\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "- levels of framework\n",
        "- macro-level\n",
        "- meso-level\n",
        "- micro level \n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "Inversen & Järvelin's Cognitive Model of Information Seeking and Retrieval ![](images/cog_model_p271.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"100%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/class_of_variables_3.png){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"100%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# Problem Statement, Purpose, & RQ\n",
        "\n",
        "## Problem Statement\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "-   gap linking LIS and NLP research\n",
        "-   new conversational search tools require new metadata quality assessment criteria\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: columns\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "[Knowns]{.yellow}\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "[Unknowns]{.yellow}\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "::::: columns\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "-   Known that metadata quality problems exist\n",
        "-   Known there are differences with sources\n",
        "-   Known that metadata can be a source of knowledge\n",
        "-   Known that noise affects LLMs and RAG\n",
        "\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: {.column width=\"50%\"}\n",
        "-   Metadata quality assessments have not included NLP perspectives\n",
        ":::\n",
        ":::::\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "## Purpose\n",
        "<br>\n",
        "\n",
        "To identify [errors and noise]{.magenta} in title and abstract content,<br>compare metadata [sources]{.yellow} for error and noise,<br>and observe the [effect on RAG]{.yellow}.\n",
        "\n",
        "## Research Questions\n",
        "\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "incremental slides!\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "::: incremental\n",
        "1.  What errors or noise may be observed in the title and abstract from a random sample of Crossref and OpenAlex?\n",
        "2.  How do Crossref and OpenAlex compare for errors and noise in the same random sample?\n",
        "3.  What is the effect of observed errors and noise on RAG retrieval and generation?\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "# Methods\n",
        "\n",
        "## \n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "- sample size 10,000 and subset\n",
        "- based on recommendations\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "break this slide into fragments with info on each method\n",
        "![](images/framework.svg){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"160%\"}\n",
        "\n",
        "## Instrument\n",
        "::: notes\n",
        "- talk more about what you did\n",
        ":::\n",
        "\n",
        "![](images/part_3_framework.svg){fig-align=\"center\" width=\"160%\"}\n",
        " \n",
        "Provide some code as example executable codeblock??\n"
